% expect-output: 0.0
% expect-output: 12.0
% expect-output: 100.0
% expect-output: 124.0
% Scenario: a rotation before setcachedevice. The glyph procedure turns
% the coordinate system a quarter turn (as an exact matrix, so the
% golden carries no trigonometric residue) and declares width 600 0 and box
% 0 0 600 400 in the turned space: in glyph space the width vector is
% 0 600 and the box the axis-aligned envelope of the turned corners,
% -400 0 0 600. At size 20 each glyph moves the current point up by 12.
% Expect: 0.0 12.0, then 100.0 124.0.
/r { 1000 mul round 1000 div } def
/Turn 7 dict dup begin
  /FontType 3 def
  /FontMatrix [0.001 0 0 0.001 0 0] def
  /Encoding StandardEncoding def
  /FontBBox [-400 0 0 600] def
  /BuildGlyph {
    pop pop
    [0 1 -1 0 0 0] concat
    600 0 0 0 600 400 setcachedevice
    0 0 moveto 600 0 lineto 300 400 lineto closepath fill
  } def
end definefont pop
/Turn findfont 20 scalefont setfont
(a) stringwidth r exch r = =
100 100 moveto (aa) show currentpoint r exch r = =
showpage
